# Regression test: electrostatics of a pair with more than 10^6 multipole point pairs (MM fragment of
# 15000 point charges, mm_box.efp, with pentacene) is computed in chunks of points shared among threads
# (heavy pairs in compute_two_body_range), with pairwise energies (ligand = pentacene). The reference energy
# is from the code before the chunking (whole pair in one piece). Energy test: the analytic gradient is the
# same as before the chunking, but the numerical gradient is not accurate enough for this 80 A wide charged
# fragment (large forces, rotation steps of 0.01 rad move its points by 0.4 A).
run_type etest
ref_energy -0.2602382439
coord points
terms elec pol
elec_damp screen
pol_damp tt
fraglib_path ../fraglib
enable_pairwise true
ligand 1

fragment mm_box
    7.000000   -37.200000   -37.200000
    7.957200   -37.200000   -37.200000
    6.760000   -36.273400   -37.200000

fragment pentacene_l
    3.636109    -0.722305     0.000000
    4.911087    -1.405659     0.000000
    6.058717    -0.722932     0.000000

fragment h2o_l
    1.200000     0.000000     3.363030
    0.447348     0.000000     2.799834
    1.952652     0.000000     2.799834
